# PREIShare — TanStack Start (React 19, Vite 8, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, npm)

- Primary agent rules live in `.cursor/rules/preishare.mdc` (see also `AGENTS.md`); this file is a short legacy summary.

- App at repo root: routes in `src/routes/`, UI in `src/components/`, tokens in `src/styles.css`, router in `src/router.tsx`.
- File-based TanStack Router: export `Route` via `createFileRoute` / `createRootRoute`; default-export functional components.
- Imports: ESM (`"type": "module"`); path aliases `#/*` and `@/*` → `src/*`. Prefer `Link` for in-app nav.
- Style with Tailwind utilities plus CSS variables from `src/styles.css` (e.g. `--sea-ink`); keep the scaffold layout unless change is justified.
- Isomorphic by default: use `createServerFn` / `createServerOnlyFn` / `createClientOnlyFn` for env boundaries. Secrets via `process.env` on server only; client config only as `VITE_*`.
- Before Start/Router/Devtools edits: `npx @tanstack/intent@latest list` then `load` matching skills. Do not edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts` by hand.
- Always use TypeScript with strict mode.
- Follow existing component patterns in `src/components`.
- No Supabase client exists yet: `src/lib/supabase.ts` is planned, not built. Do not import, create, or assume it (or any database) without team approval.
- No test runner is configured yet (no `test` script in `package.json`). Verify changes manually (`npm run build`, `npm run dev`) and state how to verify in the PR. Do not add a test framework without team approval.
